WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.603 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:09.842
Hey, I called the supermarket
chain Aldi's "Awldee's",

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:13.512
and I got the best trick
of how to say it.

00:00:13.512 --> 00:00:17.484
Someone said, "Just say Al Bundy
and drop the bun."

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:20.453
Never going to forget it.
Thank you.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:24.957
Not the same
with Nehvawda or Nehvadda.

00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:27.093
Look, there's no way to know.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:28.360
[ Soft laughter ]

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.597
We're never going to know.

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.532
I get corrected a lot on that.

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.169
The way I like to do it when
I know it's in the script

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:38.438
is not think about it
at all ahead of time.

00:00:39.705 --> 00:00:42.275
And then about 50% of the time
I'm nailing it.

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:47.347
We had a picture of Joe Biden
on a motorcycle with Jill,

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:48.647
and we said it was a Harley.

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:50.216
And one of you said,
"I can't be sure,

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.752
but that looks like
a Honda Rebel 250 CMX."

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:54.687
I think you can be sure.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.723
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.324 --> 00:01:00.593
You're coming -- You're --
Don't sell yourself short.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.530
You're coming at that
from a place of certainty.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:08.367
Ooh. Um, I showed
the Maryland flag last week.

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.170
And I-I joked down
on it a little bit.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.104
I said I tried to make
plans with it,

00:01:12.104 --> 00:01:13.639
but it was too busy.

00:01:13.639 --> 00:01:17.843
Well, the joke was on me because
I was visited in the office

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:20.179
by Maryland State Police

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.681
because I guess there's a law
on the books there

00:01:22.681 --> 00:01:26.352
that it is illegal
to burn a flag.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.721
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:41.334
We, uh, we joked that
Donald Trump would roll

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.938
into, um -- If he fell down
the stairs on an airplane,

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:46.806
he would roll down the stairs
and into a lake.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:49.476
And would have to be fished
out with a pool skimmer.

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:50.910
Many of you said that
a pool skimmer

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.813
would not be strong enough

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.314
to fish out
the former president.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:58.150
You had a lot of other...

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.819
to be honest, frankly,
cruel things

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:02.421
that would need to be used.

00:02:02.421 --> 00:02:05.858
And the only one I'll --
I'll repeat is a winch.

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:08.094
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.930
Um...

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:16.068
Our writer Seth Reiss
and his cowriter

00:02:16.068 --> 00:02:18.972
for the film "The Menu"
were on the show this week.

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.740
Will Tracy is his cowriter.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:21.807
So we had Seth and Will
on the show,

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:24.043
and everyone here
at the office agreed

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:25.745
that Will was great.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.780
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.749 --> 00:02:31.317
And, you guys,
when I put together Corrections,

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:33.619
I don't just read the comments
on "Closer Look."

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.855
I also read the comments
on the interviews.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:37.589
So, you know,
I'm going through,

00:02:37.589 --> 00:02:38.891
and I loaded that one up,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:41.727
and, uh, there was
a small problem

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:44.964
when I went to look
because, um...

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.098
Here's a riddle for you.

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:48.935
"What does a Reiss interview
on YouTube

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:51.370
have in common with a cheap
New York City apartment?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:52.972
No views."

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.008
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.145 --> 00:03:01.447
I tried to reload it.

00:03:01.447 --> 00:03:03.215
I was -- There was
an error message

00:03:03.215 --> 00:03:05.718
that said it was not
interesting enough.

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.058
Here's a picture of Reiss
during the interview.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.561
And, um, to his credit, I said,
"What are you doing?"

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.596
And he said he was gonna
plug his own ear

00:03:17.596 --> 00:03:19.299
while he was talking.

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.205
We were talking about, you know,

00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.474
Trump walked out
to a "Le Mis" song

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:30.877
at his announcement
that he was running.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:34.180
And we said it would be funny
if he was walking out to "Cats,"

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.583
you know, "Mr. Mistoffelees,"
and, you know,

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:39.752
the joke was he does look sweaty
like he's been in a cat suit.

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.587
And then, correctly,
you all said,

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.422
"Oh, but in 'Cats,'
they don't wear..."

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:45.458
'Cause I took it off
like a mascot head.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.493
And they said, "You know,
in the musical 'Cats,'

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:49.161
they're wearing, you know,
prosthetics and makeup.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:50.463
So nobody's wearing
a prosthetic head.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.332
I knew that, as well.
I just thought -- I think --

00:03:53.332 --> 00:03:55.968
And I would like -- invite
you all to think this, too.

00:03:55.968 --> 00:04:02.274
that the idea of Donald Trump
in a mascot cat head

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:06.579
is, like, almost more fun than
thinking about him in prison.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.182
Like, I'd be fine because I do
think it would be complicated

00:04:09.182 --> 00:04:10.850
for a former president
to go to jail.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:16.222
But if he got sentenced to have
to wear, like, a cat costume

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:22.462
and hand out fliers for
pet food at a -- at a mall --

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:25.331
It can be a local mall, you
know, local Palm Beach malls.

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.367
I looked. There's a lot.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:31.103
Come home after a long day.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:32.538
[ Laughs ]
Like, just Donald Trump.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.707
You wouldn't know it was him.
Well, you'd know it was him

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.408
because you'd hear, like,
a echoey, like,

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:38.511
[As Trump] "Friskies.

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.482
Fancy Feast.
Two-for-one Fancy Feast."

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:46.719
Pixar is interested
in doing a movie

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.988
about John and Jim
and the gopher.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:51.024
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.326 --> 00:04:56.962
I guess -- Well, you know
early days, you know,

00:04:56.962 --> 00:05:00.066
but the idea would be two
former NYPD police officers

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:05.438
who get reassigned to the forest
after their last assignment --

00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.105
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.105 --> 00:05:09.876
Their last assignment was
doing security for the mayor,

00:05:09.876 --> 00:05:11.210
but they got lost.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.778
They had the mayor,
and they got lost.

00:05:12.778 --> 00:05:15.481
And this is something I pitched.
It's based on a true story.

00:05:15.481 --> 00:05:18.383
Um...
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.383 --> 00:05:20.887
So, we were in --
We did our show

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.423
in Washington, DC, back in 2016.

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:26.259
And the hotel was two blocks
from the theater.

00:05:26.259 --> 00:05:29.428
And one day we walk out,
and John's leading the way.

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:31.396
Not the first day, either,
it should be noted.

00:05:31.396 --> 00:05:33.766
So we'd done a couple of shows
at the Warner Theatre.

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:36.268
And then we're out on the street
and we're walking around.

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:39.004
And we were walking for a while.
And I knew there was a problem.

00:05:39.004 --> 00:05:41.407
Bear with me for one second.
I knew there was a problem.

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:42.809
You can keep the camera there.

00:05:42.809 --> 00:05:44.543
Because all of a sudden
I was like,

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:46.979
"Wait. That's not
the flag for Washington, DC."

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.282
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.986 --> 00:05:56.989
You know what's cool about it,
though?

00:05:56.989 --> 00:05:59.792
John got us lost.

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:01.828
And Jim has never
brought it up since.

00:06:01.828 --> 00:06:04.163
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.203 --> 00:06:14.039
So, the Frankenstein --
We talked about this.

00:06:14.039 --> 00:06:16.875
And we were talking about
Frankenstein versus
Frankenstein's monster.

00:06:16.875 --> 00:06:20.312
But someone said, "It's actually
not Frankenstein's monster."

00:06:20.312 --> 00:06:23.548
You say Frankenstein's creature
or Frankenstein's creation.

00:06:23.548 --> 00:06:26.051
But at some point, guys,
look, he turned into a monster,

00:06:26.051 --> 00:06:28.654
and I think it's okay
to call him a monster, right?

00:06:28.654 --> 00:06:30.889
I mean, chucked a girl
into a pond.

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:32.458
You're a monster at that point.
I don't know what

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.026
your name was originally,
but you're allowed to --

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.594
When certain things happen,
you don't have to use

00:06:35.594 --> 00:06:37.263
the original name, right?

00:06:37.263 --> 00:06:39.097
Like, we've all allowed
ourselves to stop saying

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:41.734
"Hall-of-fame running back
O.J. Simpson."

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:45.671
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.671 --> 00:06:47.473
Also, we were, you know --
We were discussing.

00:06:47.473 --> 00:06:50.876
It seems like the villagers in
"Frankenstein" get a raw deal.

00:06:50.876 --> 00:06:54.647
You know, the whole idea, of
like, torches and pitchforks now

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:57.849
have been sort of an unruly,
unreasonable group of people.

00:06:57.849 --> 00:07:00.986
But I will say the villagers
in "Frankenstein,"

00:07:00.986 --> 00:07:03.856
I think they had every right
to be angry

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:07.526
about this creation that was
walking around their town.

00:07:07.526 --> 00:07:09.628
They had every right
to go grab their torches

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.831
and their pitchforks.
You know, they're obviously --

00:07:11.831 --> 00:07:14.734
It was an agrarian society
of farmers

00:07:14.734 --> 00:07:16.835
who didn't want, you know,
a big monster walking around

00:07:16.835 --> 00:07:19.238
chucking kids into a pond.

00:07:19.238 --> 00:07:20.740
And, you know, I mean,
it's just their bad luck

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.908
that they live near some lunatic

00:07:22.908 --> 00:07:24.776
who puts a laboratory
in a watchtower.

00:07:24.776 --> 00:07:26.745
And I'm sure when he came in,
he's like,

00:07:26.745 --> 00:07:28.181
"Oh, it'll be good for jobs."

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:31.917
You know [bleep] huge tax break.

00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:34.519
He was like, "Oh, it's gonna
bring so much to your town."

00:07:34.519 --> 00:07:36.889
And then he had, like, one job,
and he gives it to Igor.

00:07:41.827 --> 00:07:43.329
So, this is crazy.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:46.932
Obviously, I don't need
to tell fans of "Corrections."

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:48.567
We've talked a lot
about Mac Tonight

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:50.369
and the fact that he was
originally played

00:07:50.369 --> 00:07:52.771
by the fantastic actor
Doug Jones.

00:07:52.771 --> 00:07:57.042
Doug Jones himself posted
this photo of himself,

00:07:57.042 --> 00:08:00.879
young Doug Jones,
as Mac Tonight.

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:03.582
And I lost my mind
because that face and that hair

00:08:03.582 --> 00:08:06.519
looks almost exactly like
my brother when he was ten.

00:08:06.519 --> 00:08:08.421
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.556 --> 00:08:15.027
This whole time,
Mac Tonight was in the house.

00:08:15.027 --> 00:08:16.362
This is interesting.

00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:18.530
Because I said
it was a crescent moon,

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.332
and then I said
it could be either a waxing

00:08:20.332 --> 00:08:22.367
or a waning moon.

00:08:22.367 --> 00:08:26.339
So, waxing means
it's getting less.

00:08:26.339 --> 00:08:27.839
It's gone full,
and now it's getting less.

00:08:27.839 --> 00:08:30.175
Waning means it's getting more.

00:08:30.175 --> 00:08:32.644 line:0%
So this --
If it was like this,

00:08:32.644 --> 00:08:34.847 line:0%
this is a waning moon.

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.348 line:0%
Of course,
the problem with the moon

00:08:36.348 --> 00:08:37.816 line:0%
is it can't turn its head.

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:40.619 line:0%
So that would be, then,
a waxing moon, right?

00:08:40.619 --> 00:08:42.121
Is that right?
That's different. Yeah.

00:08:42.121 --> 00:08:44.022
So that's a --

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:47.292
Like it's -- "Karate Kid."

00:08:47.292 --> 00:08:49.228
"Wax on, wane off"? Right?

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:52.364
[ Laughter ]

00:08:52.364 --> 00:08:54.867
How many years has he been
your Halloween costume?

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:57.370
[ Laughter ]

00:09:01.641 --> 00:09:03.308
So...

00:09:03.308 --> 00:09:05.110
So, waxing, just...

00:09:05.110 --> 00:09:06.378
Waxing means it's going away,

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.780
and waning means
it's coming back

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:11.049
like the McRib or like
mainstream anti-Semitism.

00:09:11.049 --> 00:09:13.252
Which is -- You know what?

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:16.721
But it's a conversation starter.

00:09:16.721 --> 00:09:19.458
That's why it's okay.

00:09:19.458 --> 00:09:21.359
Just because, like,
let's have a conversation.

00:09:21.359 --> 00:09:24.396
And I think if anything
sparks a conversation,

00:09:24.396 --> 00:09:27.767
it's unimpeachable.

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:30.235
You know, I do -- I feel
a little sensitive about it,

00:09:30.235 --> 00:09:32.905
you know, because I have
a Jewish wife

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:35.074
and we're raising our kids
to be Jewish

00:09:35.074 --> 00:09:37.943
and, you know,
her entire family is Jewish.

00:09:37.943 --> 00:09:41.413
And I got to be honest, I've
spent so much time with them

00:09:41.413 --> 00:09:43.315
and I love them very much,
and the only thing

00:09:43.315 --> 00:09:46.118
they've never needed
was a conversation starter.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:48.187
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.025 --> 00:09:58.764
Oh, we paid it off
last week with --

00:09:58.764 --> 00:10:01.534
The tank top. I wore the --

00:10:01.534 --> 00:10:03.068
the Mike Scollins tank top,

00:10:03.068 --> 00:10:05.838
and some of you thought
I looked scrawny.

00:10:05.838 --> 00:10:08.707
Some of you thought
I looked ripped.

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:10.443
Nehvadda, Nehvawda.

00:10:13.278 --> 00:10:15.614
Here's a photo of it.
You can decide.

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:18.150
[ Laughter ]

00:10:23.622 --> 00:10:26.225
Here's another riddle for you,
Shoemaker.

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:30.896 line:0%
How is this photo like me
on my anniversary night?

00:10:30.896 --> 00:10:32.698 line:0%
It's untouched!

00:10:32.698 --> 00:10:34.567 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:10:39.905 --> 00:10:41.807
People had a lot
of comments about it.

00:10:41.807 --> 00:10:44.876
Someone said, "Seeing
Seth's arms feels somehow,

00:10:44.876 --> 00:10:47.913
like seeing your teacher
out at the grocery store."

00:10:47.913 --> 00:10:50.482
I obviously haven't gone
to school for a long time,

00:10:50.482 --> 00:10:53.752
but I guess teachers
are super [bleep] jacked now.

00:10:53.752 --> 00:10:56.088
[ Laughter ]

00:10:57.989 --> 00:11:00.092
I said I did -- I joked
that I did 50 pushups.

00:11:00.092 --> 00:11:03.195
And someone said, "There's
no way you can do 50 pushups."

00:11:03.195 --> 00:11:07.032
Well, not all at once.
Like, I'm not Lou Ferrigno.

00:11:07.032 --> 00:11:09.268
You break it up
over the course of the day.

00:11:13.238 --> 00:11:14.573
Some people were mad

00:11:14.573 --> 00:11:18.811
that we spoiled it
with the thumbnail pic.

00:11:18.811 --> 00:11:21.046
You know, because, you know --

00:11:21.046 --> 00:11:22.414
You could tell it, you know --

00:11:22.414 --> 00:11:24.283
If you saw the YouTube
thumbnail click,

00:11:24.283 --> 00:11:27.219
you knew that I would
eventually be in a tank top.

00:11:27.219 --> 00:11:28.520
But in those "Avengers" movies,

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:31.857
like, Thor's hammer
is in the poster.

00:11:31.857 --> 00:11:34.026
[ Laughter ]

00:11:36.328 --> 00:11:40.099
Also, I didn't want to do it,
but remember Jay and Ross

00:11:40.099 --> 00:11:43.335
were like,
"We need the clicks, baby."

00:11:43.335 --> 00:11:46.872
Those two.
"Clicks this, clicks that."

00:11:46.872 --> 00:11:50.642
Well...we've had a lovely time.

00:11:50.642 --> 00:11:54.312 line:0%
Um, let's see.

00:11:54.312 --> 00:11:56.448 line:0%
Let's see if I forgot anything.

00:11:56.448 --> 00:11:58.818 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.662 --> 00:12:11.697
[ Laughter ]

00:12:11.697 --> 00:12:13.399
See me next week!

